{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And Moses wrote this Torah</b>, from the beginning of Genesis until \"before the eyes of all Israel.\" And even though here (Deuteronomy 31:11) it is written \"you shall read this Torah before all Israel,\" which alludes to this book of Deuteronomy according to the opinion of our Sages (Sotah 41a), but in this matter he went back and explained (Deuteronomy 31:24): \"And it came to pass, when Moses had finished writing the words of this Torah in a scroll, until their conclusion,\" and this includes the entire Torah in its entirety."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:15:36.841095140Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}